We apply the distributive property repeatedly:

\begin{align*}
(x+10)(2y+10) &= x(2y+10) + 10(2y+10)\\
&= x\cdot 2y + x\cdot 10 + 10\cdot 2y + 10\cdot 10\\
&= \boxed{2xy + 10x + 20y + 100}.
\end{align*}

response:
 We can use the distributive property as follows:  $$\begin{array}{c|l}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{(x+10)(2y+10)} \\
\cline{2-2} \multicolumn{2}{l}{(x \cdot 2y+10 \cdot 2y)+(x \cdot 10+10 \cdot 10)} \\
\multicolumn{2}{l}{(2xy+20y)+(10x+100)} \\
\multicolumn{2}{l}{2xy+20y+10x+100}
\end{array}$$ Our answer is $\boxed{2xy+10x+20y+100}$. </think> <answer> 2xy+10x+20y+100 </answer>

